      "message": "[error] Line 200: 🔴 `visible: lists.length \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !IsBanned` references `lists`, which is not defined in this scope. In QML this causes a runtime `ReferenceError` and the binding won’t behave as intended, so contact-list chips may never appear (and logs get noisy). Use the actual model role/property, e.g. `visible: (ContactTags?.length ?? 0) \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !IsBanned` (or `contactListChips.lists.length \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 !IsBanned`).",
